This project builds on and installs the following software. It does not
redistribute their source in this repository; the installer fetches them.

Omarchy — https://github.com/omacom/omarchy
  Copyright (c) David Heinemeier Hansson. MIT License.
  MausOS is designed as a layer on an Omarchy installation and copies its
  conventions: the self-describing command family, config layering
  (package-owned files are never edited; user overrides live in ~/.config),
  lazy-installed agent CLIs, and the shipped agent skill.

OpenMausBot — https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot
  Copyright (c) Milind Soni. Apache License 2.0.
  MausOS runs the OpenMausBot harness server as the `mausd` user service and
  uses its web interface as the MausOS shell in Phase 0.

Hyprland — https://hyprland.org — BSD 3-Clause.
OpenCode — https://opencode.ai — MIT.
Ollama — https://ollama.com — MIT.

Proprietary agent CLIs (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI and others) are not
part of MausOS and are installed by the user under their own terms.
